# The route to the hall through both prison minigames: NOITE's street
# escape (3fstreet) starts XILINDRO, which wins (minigameWon[3]); 3fstree2
# goes back to the prison (3fprisao), its left door to the lift (3felevad)
# and the stairs to the prison escape (3farmcai), whose SERIAL wins too
# (minigameWon[2]): NOITE goes to the hall (3fhall).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fstreet --ms 222000 --input tools/play/xilindro-serial-hall.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fstreet --ms 225000 --fix all --input tools/play/xilindro-serial-hall.input
#
# The fight is xilindro-3fstreet-win.input's (+13650). 3farmcai starts at
# 94731; its video ends at 96441 and SERIAL starts at 97941. The shots are
# `tools/serial_plan.py --start 97941 --win --relative-to 94731` (a second
# in the lift picks the seed). The two versions play different games
# (BUGS.md K5): the Original hits three killers, +600, and has 4 lives left
# when the clock ends SERIAL at 217941, a win of MAKELONG(4, 500) =
# 32768004 that NOITE adds whole (BUGS.md K1, K2); the Corrigida hits one
# (shots 2 and 3 miss), keeps its 5 lives and reports a win of 500.
20000 dump street
# The Corrigida (`--fix all`) shows XILINDRO's controls screen first; Enter takes
# it down 50 ms after it opened, PORRADA stands for 2 s (the frozen intro,
# `fight_controls.start_delay_ms`) and the round then plays as the
# Original's from its start, 2050 ms later (`delay`: every later line
# moves too).
# Its keys are the new layout: S is the middle kick (the Original's Up).
